## Story Point Estimation Guide

### Fibonacci Scale: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13

| Points | What it means | Typical examples |
|--------|--------------|-----------------|
| 1 | Trivial — config toggle, label change | Enable/disable flag, update text |
| 2 | Simple — single API call, minor UI | Member lookup, balance display |
| 3 | Standard — one integration + validation | Registration sync, points credit |
| 5 | Medium — multi-step, conditional logic | Voucher issuance with rules, geofence |
| 8 | Complex — multi-system, async, retry | Full scan validation + fraud + reward |
| 13 | Very complex — full subsystem | White-label framework, AI feed engine |

### Estimation Rules
- No story should exceed 13 points — split if larger
- UAT scenarios: always 1–2 points
- NFR stories: 3–5 points (implementation complexity varies)
- Admin/config stories: 2–5 points
- Fraud/validation stories: 5–8 points (complex rule sets)
- Notification stories: 3 points (standard; 5 if multi-channel fallback)
- Reporting/dashboard stories: 3–5 points

