## Labels Convention

Use lowercase, hyphenated, comma-separated:

```
phase-1, phase-2, phase-3
registration, onboarding
scan, validation, fraud
voucher, points, rewards
notifications, engage
admin, config, reporting
nfr, security, pdpa, performance
uat, testing, go-live
integration, api, crm, pos
```

---

## Summary Field Format

```
[REQ-ID] Short descriptive title
```

Examples:
- `[FR-001] Wolf-Capillary Registration Integration`
- `[NFR-003] TLS 1.3 & AES-256 Encryption`
- `[UAT-005] Invalid QR Scan Rejection`

Keep under 100 characters. No full sentences.

---

## Quality Checklist per Story

- [ ] User story follows "As a / I want / so that" format
- [ ] Business rules listed in description
- [ ] At least 1 positive AC and 1 negative/edge case AC
- [ ] SLA / time bound in AC (e.g. "within 3 sec", "within 60 sec")
- [ ] Story Points set (Fibonacci; no blanks)
- [ ] Priority set
- [ ] Labels applied (phase + module)
- [ ] Component set
- [ ] Reporter set
- [ ] Summary starts with [REQ-ID]

---

## Epic Naming Convention

Epics should be noun phrases describing a capability area:

✅ Good:
- `Member Registration & NU Bonus`
- `QR Scan & Validation`
- `Brand-Wise Reward Issuance`
- `Admin Configuration & Reporting`
- `Non-Functional Requirements`
- `UAT & Go-Live`

❌ Avoid:
- `FR-001 to FR-005` (not descriptive)
- `Phase 1` (too broad — use as Fix Version instead)
- `All Requirements` (meaningless)

Aim for 4–8 epics per BRD. Group by functional domain, not by phase.
